{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\Privacy\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "config-without-lexicon",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Controller/AdminController.php:38 setAppValueString()",
        "lib/Controller/AdminController.php:89 setAppValueBool()",
        "lib/Settings/WhereIsYourDataSettings.php:27 getAppValueString()",
        "lib/Settings/WhoHasAccessSettings.php:56 getAppValueBool()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "The app reads and writes its app config in 4 places and registers no config lexicon, which IRegistrationContext::registerConfigLexicon() takes since Nextcloud 31. A lexicon states the type, the default and the sensitivity of each key in one place.",
        "  lib/Controller/AdminController.php:38 setAppValueString()",
        "  lib/Controller/AdminController.php:89 setAppValueBool()",
        "  lib/Settings/WhereIsYourDataSettings.php:27 getAppValueString()",
        "  lib/Settings/WhoHasAccessSettings.php:56 getAppValueBool()"
      ],
      "folds": [
        {
          "at": 4,
          "count": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "openapi-missing",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app has 5 OCS routes and no openapi.json. Clients of OCS are generated from such a specification, and nothing else tells them what these routes take and return."
      ]
    }
